_vrf_PLAT334_jin182
;
PROBLEM: Small <C-C> Benzene Dist.   C3       -C8       .       1.37 Ang.  
RESPONSE: The fluorine substituent is electron withdrawing, resulting
in smaller benzene C-C bond distances. This behavior is analogous to
previously reported structures, such as CCDC no. 200653.
;
_vrf_PLAT342_jin182
;
PROBLEM: Low Bond Precision on  C-C Bonds ...............     0.0105 Ang.  
RESPONSE: This is the best possible bond precision for the collected data.
;
_vrf_PLAT906_jin182
;
PROBLEM: Large K Value in the Analysis of Variance ......      9.540 Check 
RESPONSE: Usually data integration algorithms underestimate the background
 and produces slightly elevated values of Fo, resulting in higher Fo/Fc
 values. These are most pronounced for the weakest intensities.
;
_vrf_PLAT910_jin182
;
PROBLEM: Missing # of FCF Reflection(s) Below Theta(Min).         12 Note  
RESPONSE: These reflections were collected but excluded during integration.
;
_vrf_PLAT976_jin182
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.02Ang From N1      .      -0.51 eA-3  
RESPONSE: This residual density is less than that of the largest
peak/hole (0.6/-0.7) and is considered noise.
;
_vrf_PLAT977_jin182
;
PROBLEM: Check Negative Difference Density on H1C       .      -0.41 eA-3  
RESPONSE: The chemical formula is known from the synthesis. All H atoms were
 placed in calculated idealized positions that are consistent with the
 hybridization of the C and N atoms. All H atoms in the model are needed to
 balance the charge.
